@startuml holler-3-states
title The two state machines inside a message

skinparam shadowing false

state "The message in the queue (HollerEntry.Stage)" as stages {
    [*] --> Queued : show()
    Queued : shown by your code, not drawn yet
    Queued --> Visible : the host draws it\n(a free place among maxVisible)
    Visible : on screen, enter animation played
    Visible --> Visible : replaced by a show()\nwith the same key
    Visible --> Leaving : dismissed for any reason
    Leaving : exit animation playing,\nits key is free again
    Queued --> [*] : dismissed or left undrawn\n(removed at once)
    Leaving --> [*] : exit animation ended
}

state "Its countdown (HollerTimer.Phase)" as phases {
    [*] --> Counting : the card appears
    Counting : time is passing
    Counting --> Paused : dragged, pressed or hovered,\nor covered by a newer message in a pile
    Paused : held for a moment
    Paused --> Counting : let go,\nor in front again
    Counting --> Stopped : expanded by the user\n(as stoppableBy allows)
    Stopped : stays until closed;\nbar and countdown are gone
    Counting --> Finished : the full time has passed
    Finished : reports Timeout,\nwhich makes the message leave
    Finished --> [*]
    Stopped --> [*] : the message is closed
}

note bottom of phases
    An Infinite message has no countdown at all.
    A queued message has no timer yet:
    it starts when the message becomes visible.
end note

@enduml
